    excerpt: `Stroke is one of the leading causes of death and long-term disability across the world. Every year, millions of people suffer a stroke, and many are left with permanent disabilities that affect their ability to speak, walk, work, or perform daily activities independently. The good news is that with timely recognition, emergency treatment, and proper rehabilitation, many stroke patients can recover successfully and regain a good quality of life.`,
