<p>Patients with persistent nerve compression or severe symptoms despite non-surgical treatment may be considered for procedures or surgery. Endoscopic spine surgery is a minimally invasive option for selected conditions and may involve smaller incisions, less tissue disruption, reduced postoperative discomfort, shorter hospital stays, and faster recovery than some traditional procedures.</p>
