    excerpt: `Parkinson’s disease is a progressive neurological disorder that primarily affects movement. It can cause tremors, stiffness, slowness of movement, walking difficulties, and balance problems. However, Parkinson’s disease is more than a movement disorder. It can also affect sleep, mood, speech, digestion, memory, and daily activities.`,
