    excerpt: `Rheumatoid arthritis is a chronic autoimmune condition that primarily affects the joints but can also involve other parts of the body. Unlike ordinary joint pain caused by overuse or aging, rheumatoid arthritis occurs when the immune system mistakenly attacks the body's own tissues, particularly the lining of the joints. This can lead to inflammation, pain, swelling, stiffness, and, if left untreated, progressive joint damage.`,
    category: 'Rheumatology',
