    title: `Gout: Causes, Symptoms, Diagnosis, Treatment and How to Prevent Recurrent Attacks`,
    excerpt: `Gout is a common form of inflammatory arthritis that can cause sudden and intense joint pain, swelling, warmth, and redness. It develops when excess uric acid builds up in the body and forms sharp crystals within or around a joint.`,
    category: 'Rheumatology',
