    title: `Lupus (SLE): Symptoms, Causes, Diagnosis and Treatment Options`,
    excerpt: `Systemic lupus erythematosus, commonly known as lupus or SLE, is a chronic autoimmune disease that can affect different parts of the body. In lupus, the immune system becomes abnormally activated and attacks the body's own healthy tissues, resulting in inflammation.`,
    category: 'Rheumatology',
