    excerpt: `Knee arthritis can gradually change the way a person walks, exercises, works, and performs everyday activities. In the early stages, symptoms may be manageable with non-surgical treatment. However, advanced arthritis can cause persistent pain and stiffness that significantly affect quality of life.`,
    category: 'Orthopedics',
