    excerpt: `Irregular periods are a common concern among women of different age groups. A menstrual cycle does not always follow the same pattern every month, and occasional changes may happen because of stress, changes in weight, travel, exercise, or other temporary factors. However, frequent or persistent changes in the menstrual cycle may sometimes indicate an underlying health condition that needs medical attention.`,
