    excerpt: `Polycystic ovary syndrome, commonly known as PCOS, is a hormonal condition that can affect women during their reproductive years. It may influence menstrual cycles, ovulation, metabolism, skin, hair growth, and fertility. Although PCOS is common, its symptoms can vary significantly from one woman to another.`,
