    excerpt: `Menstrual bleeding can vary from woman to woman, but unusually heavy or prolonged periods may affect daily activities and overall health. Heavy menstrual bleeding is not simply an inconvenience. When it occurs repeatedly, it can lead to tiredness, weakness, anemia, and reduced quality of life.`,
    category: 'Gynecology',
