    excerpt: `Knee pain can gradually change the way a person lives. Simple activities such as walking, climbing stairs, getting up from a chair, or spending time with family may become uncomfortable. When advanced knee arthritis causes persistent pain and limits daily activities despite non-surgical treatment, knee replacement may be considered.`,
