    excerpt: `An anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) tear is one of the most common and important knee ligament injuries, particularly among people who participate in sports involving sudden changes in direction, jumping, pivoting or rapid stopping. However, an ACL injury can also occur during a fall, road accident or everyday activity.`,
